      "id": "LUG-16",
      "plano": "terminal86",
      "provisional": false,
      "nota": "<p><strong>Location:</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.lIohEQe1KFTOCQ0U]{The Terminal 86 Grain Elevator}<br><strong>Scenes:</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.C7cxKf7kcAELzuJ1.JournalEntryPage.hAX2tLfjRPJ2o4Tr]{A3-E03 · Face to Face with Krell}</p>\n<p><strong>Arrival (A3-E03, Night 7, midnight).</strong> “The service stair zigzags up the outside of the silo to a long, narrow gallery of sheet metal and dirty glass. Inside, a stopped conveyor belt runs end to end.” Krell expects David to come in through the west <strong>sheet-metal door</strong>; the coterie decides whether to bring him and who goes up with him. At the far end, to the east, is the <strong>open loading door</strong> over the bay (an open door: the Storyteller can close it), and in front of it, the <strong>chair</strong> with the hostage (tile <code>tile-silla-madera</code>; Krell pushes it toward the edge if he sees the whole coterie). Krell waits sitting on the belt. The scene has <strong>rain and wind weather</strong>: it blows in through the loading door.</p>\n<p><strong>Heights (one floor per map).</strong> The gallery is <strong>40 m</strong> above the terminal yard (the height of the silos). The loading door at the end opens over the water, <strong>30 m</strong> down (A3-E03). What you see through the windows and through the stair grating is painted exterior: you don&#39;t walk there, you reach it through regions.</p>\n<p><strong>The three approaches</strong> (Dexterity + Stealth Diff. 4 vs. Krell&#39;s Wits + Awareness, 7 dice):</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The outside stair</strong> (the one David uses): region “Go down the service stair” on the flight that keeps going down; the arrival is the top landing, in front of the door.</li>\n<li><strong>The inside of the neighboring silo</strong> (Athletics Diff. 3 to climb): comes out through the floor loading hatch marked in the south aisle, about 8 m from the chair. A PC hidden there reaches the chair with Dexterity + Stealth Diff. 4.</li>\n<li><strong>The water</strong> (a boat below the loading door): region in front of the loading door, on the outside.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>The loading door.</strong> Anyone who falls through it takes 4 bashing damage on hitting the water, thirty meters down. In combat, Krell tries to throw his opponents out through it (Strength + Brawl vs. Dexterity + Athletics); if he drops to half his Health, he jumps himself and disappears. The region outside the loading door is the fall.</p>\n<p><strong>Off the map.</strong> Gale&#39;s drone films from 200 m away, without sound: it isn&#39;t on the map.</p>\n\n<p class=\"sbn-moviles\">The movable furniture (1) are unlocked tiles: they can be moved, knocked over or used as a barricade.</p>\n<div class=\"sbn-figuras\"><p><strong>Placed tokens.</strong> Hidden ones are revealed from the token layer; the ones that depend on how the night went say when.</p><ul><li>@UUID[Actor.Y53IKZpt8sl2sl65]{August Krell} (A3-E03): Sitting on the belt, his gray coat open. The hostage from A3-E01 is tied to the chair by the loading door: put their token there.</li></ul></div>\n<p class=\"sbn-pendientes\"><strong>Exits without a map (grey region, leads nowhere):</strong> Go down the service stair (40 m to the yard) · Neighboring silo hatch (climb up the inside: Athletics Diff. 3) · Outside the loading door: fall to the water, 30 m (4 bashing) / arrival from the boat.</p>",
      "moviles": []
    }
  },
